<h1 id="tactile-based-multimodal-fusion-in-embodied-intelligence-survey">Tactile-based Multimodal Fusion in Embodied Intelligence Survey</h1>
<blockquote>
<p><strong>Source</strong>: jiqizhixin.com (WeChat) | mp.weixin.qq.com/s/5uWwLRaFzQByC9fsj1ly7w<br />
<strong>Date</strong>: 2026-04-07<br />
<strong>Tags</strong>: embodied-intelligence, tactile-sensing, multimodal-fusion, robotics, VLA<br />
<strong>Rating</strong>: ⭐⭐⭐⭐⭐<br />
<strong>Paper</strong>: https://www.researchgate.net/publication/403306640<br />
<strong>GitHub</strong>: https://github.com/Wayne-coding/Multimodal-Tactile-Sensing-and-Fusion</p>
</blockquote>
<hr />
<h2 id="core-thesis">Core Thesis</h2>
<p>Tactile sensing is the missing piece in embodied intelligence. As LLMs/WAMs/VLAs explode, fusing tactile feedback with vision and language is the inevitable path to bridging physical interaction with high-level semantic reasoning. This survey (HKUST-GZ × LinkerBot × multiple universities) provides the most comprehensive taxonomy to date.</p>
