<h2 id="three-algorithmic-paradigms">Three Algorithmic Paradigms</h2>
<h3 id="1-multimodal-perception-recognition">1. Multimodal Perception &amp; Recognition</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Object recognition</strong>: VHTformer uses Transformer joint query — works even on transparent/occluded objects</li>
<li><strong>Material recognition</strong>: UniTouch enables zero-shot via CLIP text prompts (no training needed for new materials)</li>
<li><strong>Grasp stability prediction</strong>: Real-time tactile feedback (slip, force distribution) for closed-loop control</li>
<li><strong>Cross-modal retrieval</strong>: Evaluate alignment quality by matching tactile→visual/language</li>
</ul>
<h3 id="2-cross-modal-generation-translation">2. Cross-modal Generation &amp; Translation</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Vision↔Tactile</strong>: Generate tactile deformation from photos (rock texture), or infer visual texture from touch</li>
<li><strong>Language→Tactile</strong>: Text-to-Tactile synthesis — generate physical tactile data from text description alone</li>
<li><strong>Tactile→Language</strong>: VTV-LLM generates natural language captions for contact experiences</li>
</ul>
<h3 id="3-multimodal-interaction-control">3. Multimodal Interaction &amp; Control</h3>
<ul>
<li><strong>Perception-driven manipulation</strong>: DexTac uses contact region prompts for high-precision tasks (syringe handling)</li>
<li><strong>Language-instructed VLA</strong>: Abstract commands ("gently grasp that soft object") → joint semantic + geometric + tactile → continuous actions</li>
</ul>
