<h2 id="data-evolution">Data Evolution</h2>
<pre><code>T-V datasets (lab-controlled, e.g. VT Dataset)
  → T-V datasets (in-the-wild, e.g. Touch in the Wild)
  → T-L datasets (semantic grounding, e.g. STOLA)
  → T-V-L datasets (100K+ tri-modal, e.g. Touch100k)
  → T-V-O datasets (+ action/audio/proprioception, e.g. OmniViTac)
</code></pre>
<h2 id="four-core-challenges">Four Core Challenges</h2>
<ol>
<li><strong>Data fragmentation</strong>: Task-specific, sensor-dependent, far smaller than V-L resources</li>
<li><strong>Modal misalignment</strong>: Sparse tactile vs dense visual/language, sensor drift, occlusion</li>
<li><strong>HW integration</strong>: Diverse form factors, no standard interface, durability/power limits</li>
<li><strong>No unified benchmark</strong>: Fragmented metrics, no end-to-end embodied evaluation</li>
</ol>
<h2 id="future-directions">Future Directions</h2>
<ul>
<li>Unified large-scale datasets (break data bottleneck)</li>
<li>Hierarchical fusion architecture (tactile as foundational modality)</li>
<li>Flexible, durable bionic tactile skin with edge processing</li>
<li>Tactile feedback as continuous supervision signal in decision loops</li>
</ul>
